---
title: Three ways out
elements:
  - { id: mug, type: path, closed: true, points: [[310, 170], [490, 170], [510, 480], [290, 480]] }
  - { id: brew, type: path, closed: true, points: [[318, 178], [482, 178], [497, 430], [303, 430]], style: { fill: "#d0865f" } }
  - { id: a_cond, type: arrow, from: { x: 515, y: 280 }, to: { x: 700, y: 280 }, style: { color: "#b5482e" } }
  - { id: lab_cond, type: label, text: Conduction, attach_to: a_cond, side: right, style: { color: "#b5482e" } }
  - { id: a_conv, type: arrow, from: { x: 400, y: 500 }, to: { x: 400, y: 650 }, style: { color: "#b5482e" } }
  - { id: lab_conv, type: label, text: Convection, attach_to: a_conv, side: left, style: { color: "#b5482e" } }
  - { id: a_rad, type: arrow, from: { x: 520, y: 420 }, to: { x: 675, y: 530 }, style: { color: "#b5482e" } }
  - { id: lab_rad, type: label, text: Radiation, attach_to: a_rad, side: right, style: { color: "#b5482e" } }
commands:
  - draw: [mug]
    speak: "Coffee poured at ninety degrees is undrinkably hot; in an open mug it is lukewarm within the hour."
  - draw: [brew]
    speak: "In a flask the same coffee is still hot at supper — and the flask has no power, no battery, nothing added."
  - draw: [a_cond, lab_cond]
    speak: "So whatever it does, it does by closing the ways heat leaves. Conduction is the first: heat walks out through the ceramic, molecule bumping molecule."
  - draw: [a_conv, lab_conv]
    speak: "Convection is the second, off the top: warm air lifts away, and every gram of water that evaporates carries off the energy it took to boil it."
  - draw: [a_rad, lab_rad]
    speak: "The third is radiation — anything warmer than its surroundings glows in the infrared, coffee and hand alike."
  - highlight: { target: [a_conv], effect: glow }
    speak: "The open top is the widest door, which is why a saucer laid over the cup does more than it looks like it should."
  - point: { at: { ref: mug }, gesture: circle }
    speak: "None of this is a fault in the mug. All three are simply what physics does to anything warm."
  - focus: { target: [a_cond, a_conv, a_rad] }
    speak: "Three doors, then — and a flask cannot add heat, so the only thing it can possibly do is shut them."
---
title: How the flask shuts them
elements:
  - { id: outer, type: path, closed: true, points: [[300, 150], [640, 150], [640, 620], [300, 620]] }
  - { id: inner, type: path, closed: true, points: [[350, 195], [590, 195], [590, 620], [350, 620]] }
  - { id: brew2, type: path, closed: true, points: [[358, 203], [582, 203], [582, 555], [358, 555]], style: { fill: "#d0865f" } }
  - { id: vacuum_gap, type: shape, shape: rect, x: 615, y: 470, width: 42, height: 190, style: { color: "#2f6b8f", dash: true } }
  - { id: lab_vac, type: label, text: Vacuum, attach_to: vacuum_gap, side: right, style: { color: "#2f6b8f" } }
  - { id: silver_in, type: path, points: [[592, 350], [592, 210]], style: { color: "#2f6b8f" } }
  - { id: silver_in_l, type: path, points: [[348, 350], [348, 210]], style: { color: "#2f6b8f" } }
  - { id: silver_out_l, type: path, points: [[302, 350], [302, 210]], style: { color: "#2f6b8f" } }
  - { id: silver_out, type: path, points: [[638, 350], [638, 210]], style: { color: "#2f6b8f" } }
  - { id: lab_sil, type: label, text: Silvered, attach_to: silver_out, side: right, style: { color: "#2f6b8f" } }
  - { id: stopper, type: shape, shape: rect, x: 470, y: 650, width: 260, height: 60, style: { color: "#2f6b8f" } }
  - { id: lab_stopper, type: label, text: Stopper, attach_to: stopper, side: above, style: { color: "#2f6b8f" } }
commands:
  - draw: [outer]
    speak: "Now that the three doors have names, here is what the flask does to them: it is two bottles, one inside the other."
  - draw: [inner, brew2]
    speak: "The coffee only ever touches the inner one."
  - draw: [vacuum_gap, lab_vac]
    speak: "The air between them is pumped out. With almost nothing left in that gap there is nothing to conduct heat across it and nothing to circulate — one emptiness closes two of the three doors."
  - draw: [silver_in, silver_out, silver_in_l, silver_out_l, lab_sil]
    speak: "Radiation crosses a vacuum perfectly happily, so both facing surfaces are silvered: infrared arrives at a mirror and is sent straight back into the coffee."
  - draw: [stopper, lab_stopper]
    speak: "And the stopper seals the top, where the steam was leaving."
  - focus: { target: [outer, inner] }
    speak: "James Dewar built the first one of these in 1892, to hold gases he had just learned to liquefy — and never patented it."
  - point: { at: { ref: outer }, gesture: circle }
    speak: "A glassblower who had made flasks for his laboratory put it on the market as the Thermos; Dewar went to court over it and lost."
  - highlight: { target: [vacuum_gap, silver_in, silver_out, stopper], effect: glow }
    speak: "Three ways out, three of them closed, and not one watt spent doing it."
---
title: What is left
template: generic_axes_diagram
params:
  title: Coffee, cooling
  x_label: Time
  y_label: Temperature
  curves:
    - { expression: "20 + 70*exp(-x/4)", label: Mug, color: demand }
    - { expression: "20 + 70*exp(-x/140)", label: Flask, color: supply }
  points:
    - { x: 8, y: 29.5, label: "30 °C after 1 hour" }
    - { x: 50, y: 69, label: "69 °C after 6 hours" }
elements:
  - { id: flask_pic, type: inset, of: How the flask shuts them }
commands:
  - draw: [flask_pic]
    speak: "Now that the doors are shut, watch what the two vessels actually do."
  - draw: [title, axes, x_label, y_label]
  - draw: [curve_0, label_curve_0]
    speak: "Ninety degrees in an open mug: the curve falls off a cliff, because all three doors are wide open."
  - draw: [point_0, point_label_0]
    speak: "An hour in, it is down to thirty degrees — barely warm."
  - draw: [curve_1, label_curve_1]
    speak: "The flask starts at the same ninety and takes all day to do what the mug did in an hour."
  - draw: [point_1, point_label_1]
    speak: "Six hours later it is still at sixty-nine."
  - highlight: { target: [curve_1], effect: glow }
    speak: "But look at the slope: it does fall. A perfect flask would be a flat line, and this is not one."
  - move: { target: flask_pic, scale: 4, to: { x: 480, y: 400 } }
  - focus: { target: [flask_pic] }
    speak: "The two bottles have to meet somewhere, and they meet at the neck — a ring of glass that conducts, under a stopper that is not a vacuum."
  - point: { at: { ref: flask_pic, anchor: stopper } }
  - move: { target: flask_pic, scale: 0.25, to: { x: 900, y: 670 } }
  - highlight: { target: [curve_0, curve_1], effect: glow }
    speak: "So a flask never keeps anything hot. It only makes the way out long — and that alone turns one hour into a day."
